THE MOST IMPORTANT THING IS,
TO ME, SEEING ALL THE DESIGNERS.

284
00:12:44,368 --> 00:12:46,571
THANK YOU FOR ALL
YOUR BEAUTIFUL FLOWERS.

285
00:12:46,571 --> 00:12:48,573
I KNOW WE HAVE TO BE BACK
ON TIME AT 4:30,

286
00:12:48,573 --> 00:12:49,807
BUT THAT'S THE MOST
IMPORTANT THING TO ME.

287
00:12:59,317 --> 00:13:00,918
(speaking Thai)

288
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:05,256
JADE IS AN HOUR
AND TEN MINUTES LATE.

289
00:13:05,256 --> 00:13:06,691
(door creaks)

290
00:13:06,691 --> 00:13:09,694
WHEN JADE WALKED INTO THIS ROOM,
LET ME TELL YOU,

291
00:13:09,694 --> 00:13:12,463
SHE HAD SOME GLASSES ON,
TRYING TO BE INCOGNITO.

292
00:13:12,463 --> 00:13:13,965
OH, MY GOD,
IT WAS HILARIOUS.

293
00:13:13,965 --> 00:13:16,701
ALL THE GIRLS ARE LOOKING AT ME
LIKE...

294
00:13:16,701 --> 00:13:18,903
AND I'M LIKE,
"BITCHES, PLEASE, OKAY?

295
00:13:18,903 --> 00:13:19,971
RELAX YOURSELF."

296
00:13:45,630 --> 00:13:47,765
ALL I GOT TO SAY
TO THAT DESIGNER IS,

297
00:13:47,765 --> 00:13:51,235
"YOU TRY TRAVELING AROUND
IN A TUK-TUK WITH NO DOORS,

298
00:13:51,235 --> 00:13:53,638
"HUMID OUTSIDE AND HOT,
AND SEE HOW YOUR APPEARANCE LOOK

299
00:13:53,638 --> 00:13:54,505
BY THE END OF THE DAY."

300
00:14:02,647 --> 00:14:04,248
I WISH SHE WOULD HAVE SAID,

301
00:14:04,248 --> 00:14:06,484
"JADE REALLY HAS SUPERMODEL
STATUS TALENTS."

302
00:14:06,484 --> 00:14:07,518
YOU KNOW?
I WANT TO HEAR THAT.

303
00:14:28,606 --> 00:14:29,840
I'M SO SORRY.

304
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:31,809
GOOD LUCK AND GOOD-BYE.

305
00:14:31,809 --> 00:14:33,811
THAT'S LIKE TAKING A KID
TO A CANDY STORE

306
00:14:33,811 --> 00:14:35,713
AND SAYING,
"YOU CAN'T HAVE THE CANDY."

307
00:14:35,713 --> 00:14:36,948
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

308
00:14:36,948 --> 00:14:38,182
SHUT YOUR MOUTH.

309
00:14:38,182 --> 00:14:39,517
OH, MY GOSH.

310
00:14:39,517 --> 00:14:41,719
SHUT YOUR MOUTH AND SAY
IT AIN'T SO.

311
00:14:41,719 --> 00:14:43,187
YOU GOT THE BRAS, TOO.

312
00:14:43,187 --> 00:14:44,488
I AIN'T GOT NOTHING.

313
00:14:44,488 --> 00:14:45,957
I MEAN, YOU WOULD HAVE
HAD THE BRAS.

314
00:14:45,957 --> 00:14:47,692
SHUT UP.

315
00:14:47,692 --> 00:14:48,726
PLEASE PUNCH ME IN THE FACE.

316
00:14:48,726 --> 00:14:49,961
BAM.

317
00:14:49,961 --> 00:14:52,263
THAT SUCKS FOR DANIELLE.

318
00:14:52,263 --> 00:14:53,264
I FEEL VERY BAD FOR HER.

319
00:14:54,565 --> 00:14:55,900
TYRA MAIL.

320
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:58,536
"DOES THIS COMPETITION
EVER GET SO DIFFICULT

321
00:14:58,536 --> 00:14:59,804
THAT YOU JUST
WANT TO SAY"...

322
00:14:59,804 --> 00:15:01,472
(laughing)

323
00:15:01,472 --> 00:15:03,774
I'M LIKE, WHAT ARE WE
ABOUT TO BE DOING?

324
00:15:03,774 --> 00:15:06,510
BUT, YOU KNOW, IT'S NOT
PRONOUNCED THE F-WORD,

325
00:15:06,510 --> 00:15:09,880
IT'S ACTUALLY "POO-KET,"
AND SARA HAS A BOOK ON THAILAND,

326
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:11,616
SO SHE WENT AND LOOKED UP
"PHUKET."

327
00:15:11,616 --> 00:15:13,684
PHUKET PROVINCE.

328
00:15:13,684 --> 00:15:14,885
YEP.

329
00:15:14,885 --> 00:15:18,356
- DIVING AND SNORKELING.
- DIVING AND SNORKELING!

330
00:15:18,356 --> 00:15:19,890
- THAT'S WHAT THEY SAY?
- YEAH!

331
00:15:19,890 --> 00:15:21,892
WE GOING TO THE OCEAN,
BREAK IT DOWN.

332
00:15:21,892 --> 00:15:23,227
WE GOING TO THE OCEAN.

333
00:15:23,227 --> 00:15:24,729
WE'RE HEADED TO PHUKET,

334
00:15:24,729 --> 00:15:28,399
AND THAT IS, LIKE, THE BEST
TROPICAL LOCATION EVER.

335
00:15:28,399 --> 00:15:32,970
IT'S LIKE THE MIAMI BEACH,
RIO DE JANEIRO OF ASIA.

336
00:15:35,906 --> 00:15:37,608
WHEN WE ARRIVE
AT THE AIRPORT,

337
00:15:37,608 --> 00:15:39,410
I'M LIKE A LITTLE KID
ON CHRISTMAS.

338
00:15:39,410 --> 00:15:40,945
LIKE, I WANT TO GET THERE.

339
00:15:44,582 --> 00:15:49,520
I WAS LIKE, "OH, MY GOD,
WE'RE GOING TO PARADISE."

340
00:15:53,424 --> 00:15:56,927
I THINK THAT I HAD A REALLY
BAD DAY ON THE GO-SEES,

341
00:15:56,927 --> 00:15:58,896
BUT HERE IN PHUKET,
IT'S LIKE,

342
00:15:58,896 --> 00:16:01,832
ALL THE STRESSES OF
THE COMPETITION AND EVERYTHING

343
00:16:01,832 --> 00:16:05,236
JUST KIND OF DISAPPEAR,
AT LEAST FOR THE TIME BEING.

344
00:16:05,236 --> 00:16:06,504
JADE DOESN'T CARE
ABOUT ANYTHING

345
00:16:06,504 --> 00:16:08,706
AS LONG AS SHE'S
GOING TO THE OCEAN.

346
00:16:08,706 --> 00:16:10,641
Y'ALL KNOW I'VE BEEN DYING
TO GO TO THE OCEAN.

347
00:16:10,641 --> 00:16:13,511
LIKE, THE WATER AND JADE,
WE MIX, YOU KNOW?

348
00:16:13,511 --> 00:16:14,412
THAT'S JUST...
I LOVE IT.

349
00:16:16,914 --> 00:16:18,315
HOME SWEET HOME.

350
00:16:18,315 --> 00:16:20,751
HOLY COW.

351
00:16:20,751 --> 00:16:22,953
WE GET TO OUR VILLA WHERE
WE'RE GONNA BE STAYING.

352
00:16:22,953 --> 00:16:26,424
WE GET INSIDE,
AND IT'S ABSOLUTELY AMAZING.

353
00:16:26,424 --> 00:16:28,225
WOW.

354
00:16:28,225 --> 00:16:29,193
IT'S GORGEOUS.

355
00:16:29,193 --> 00:16:30,428
A TROPICAL PARADISE.

356
00:16:30,428 --> 00:16:31,962
IT'S JUST GORGEOUS.

357
00:16:31,962 --> 00:16:33,631
YOU CAN SEE THE OCEAN
FROM HERE.

358
00:16:33,631 --> 00:16:35,633
- OH, IT'S GONNA BE SO PRETTY.
- WOW.

359
00:16:35,633 --> 00:16:37,568
- THIS IS AWESOME.
- IT'S UNBELIEVABLE.

360
00:16:37,568 --> 00:16:39,804
IT'S THE MOST BEAUTIFUL PLACE
I HAVE EVER BEEN IN MY LIFE,

361
00:16:39,804 --> 00:16:40,871
AND I DON'T
EVER WANT TO LEAVE.

362
00:16:43,474 --> 00:16:45,376
I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS IS GONNA BE
OVER IN A WEEK.

363
00:16:45,376 --> 00:16:46,844
BACK TO, LIKE, REAL LIFE.

364
00:16:46,844 --> 00:16:49,313
WITH SARA,
THIS IS HER FIRST TIME EVER

365
00:16:49,313 --> 00:16:51,348
DOING ANY TYPE
OF MODELING.

366
00:16:51,348 --> 00:16:52,283
IT'S ALL VERY NEW TO HER.

367
00:16:52,283 --> 00:16:53,651
WHAT A RIDE.

368
00:16:53,651 --> 00:16:54,952
EVERYTHING HERE IS WILD.

369
00:16:54,952 --> 00:16:56,687
BEYOND MY WILDEST DREAMS,
MAN.

370
00:16:56,687 --> 00:17:01,225
I REALLY NEED TO SHOW HOW MUCH
I DO WANT IT AND HOW, YOU KNOW,

371
00:17:01,225 --> 00:17:02,927
THIS ISN'T SOMETHING THAT JUST
FELL INTO MY LAP.

372
00:17:02,927 --> 00:17:04,361
EVERYTHING HAPPENS
FOR A REASON.

373
00:17:04,361 --> 00:17:05,429
'CAUSE I WOULD NOT
BE HERE RIGHT NOW.

374
00:17:08,299 --> 00:17:11,769
IT'S CRAZY FOR ME TO REALIZE
THAT I'M IN THE FINAL FOUR.

375
00:17:11,769 --> 00:17:13,537
YOU GUYS WANT TO EAT INSIDE
OR OUTSIDE?

376
00:17:13,537 --> 00:17:14,704
EAT OUTSIDE.

377
00:17:14,704 --> 00:17:17,974
I FEEL, LIKE, VERY,
VERY ANNOYED WITH SARA,

378
00:17:17,974 --> 00:17:22,246
BECAUSE I REALLY FEEL LIKE
THIS IS NOT HER FIRST CHOICE.

379
00:17:22,246 --> 00:17:23,748
THIS ISN'T HER PASSION.

380
00:17:23,748 --> 00:17:25,583
SHE WAS THIS CLOSE
TO BEING A LAWYER

381
00:17:25,583 --> 00:17:27,718
AND HAD A CAREER
SET OUT FOR HER.

382
00:17:27,718 --> 00:17:29,620
IF SHE HADN'T BEEN PICKED OUT
IN A MALL,

383
00:17:29,620 --> 00:17:30,921
SHE WOULDN'T BE HERE.

384
00:17:30,921 --> 00:17:32,256
I FEEL LIKE
A BITCH.

385
00:17:32,256 --> 00:17:33,723
BUT I'M JUST LIKE...

386
00:17:33,723 --> 00:17:34,925
BUT I'M LIKE, THIS IS WHAT
IT COMES DOWN TO.

387
00:17:34,925 --> 00:17:37,561
THIS IS COMPETING
FOR SOMETHING THAT'S, LIKE,

388
00:17:37,561 --> 00:17:38,829
YOU'RE GONNA BE
LIVING WITH

389
00:17:38,829 --> 00:17:40,698
THE REST OF YOUR LIFE,
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

390
00:17:40,698 --> 00:17:43,834
I CAN'T FOCUS ON HER SITUATION.
I GOTTA- I HAVE TO DO ME.

391
00:17:43,834 --> 00:17:45,202
YOU KNOW WHAT I'M SAYING?
AND SO...

392
00:17:45,202 --> 00:17:46,504
WORKSHOP AND KEEP GOING.

393
00:17:46,504 --> 00:17:50,207
THE REASON WHY IT HIT ME NOW
IS BECAUSE, LIKE,

394
00:17:50,207 --> 00:17:51,675
SHE COPIES OFF OF ME.

395
00:17:51,675 --> 00:17:53,644
I WANT TO START DOING
A LITTLE BIT OF THE THING

396
00:17:53,644 --> 00:17:55,379
THAT JOANIE JUST DID.

397
00:17:59,817 --> 00:18:02,286
I'M JUST GONNA START DOING
THINGS WRONG ON PURPOSE,

398
00:18:02,286 --> 00:18:03,287
- MAYBE SHE...
- (laughing)

399
00:18:03,287 --> 00:18:04,655
(laughs)

400
00:18:04,655 --> 00:18:06,857
WHEN IT COMES TO THIS
COMPETITION, LIKE,

401
00:18:06,857 --> 00:18:11,428
I JUST DON'T FEEL LIKE
SHE SHOULD BE HERE ANYMORE.

402
00:18:16,967 --> 00:18:18,636
♪♪♪

403
00:18:18,636 --> 00:18:20,371
TYRA MAIL!

404
00:18:20,371 --> 00:18:22,306
AND IT CAME OUT
OF THIS COCONUT.

405
00:18:22,306 --> 00:18:24,341
"THE COMPETITION
IS GETTING DIRTY.

406
00:18:24,341 --> 00:18:26,610
NOW IT'S TIME
TO TAKE A BATH."

407
00:18:26,610 --> 00:18:27,745
RUNNING WATERFALLS.

408
00:18:27,745 --> 00:18:29,580
THAT'S WHAT I THINK--
CLEAN, WATERFALLS.

409
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:31,248
WHAT ARE WE FIXIN'
TO BE DOING?

410
00:18:31,248 --> 00:18:32,950
IT'S LIKE, YOU KNOW,
THE TYRA MAILS KIND OF GIVE YOU

411
00:18:32,950 --> 00:18:34,485
LITTLE CLUES AND HINTS

412
00:18:34,485 --> 00:18:35,619
AS TO WHAT
YOU'RE GONNA BE DOING.

413
00:18:35,619 --> 00:18:37,221
WE SHOULD WAIT
AND SEE TOMORROW.

414
00:18:48,265 --> 00:18:50,301
HELLO.

415
00:18:50,301 --> 00:18:51,368
HOW ARE YOU?

416
00:18:51,368 --> 00:18:52,770
GOOD, HOW ARE YOU?

417
00:18:52,770 --> 00:18:54,471
- HUG.
- OKAY.

418
00:18:54,471 --> 00:18:55,573
Y'ALL LOOK SO PRETTY.

419
00:18:55,573 --> 00:18:56,807
THANK YOU.

420
00:18:56,807 --> 00:18:58,709
JUST CUTE ON YOUR OWN,
JUST FOR NO REASON.

421
00:18:58,709 --> 00:19:01,478
WELL, WE JUST LIKE TO SIT UP
AND CHILL, BE CHILL.

422
00:19:01,478 --> 00:19:05,182
WE WAKE UP, AND I SEE
TYRA BANKS, AND I'M LIKE,

423
00:19:05,182 --> 00:19:06,283
"TYRA IS IN OUR HUT."

424
00:19:06,283 --> 00:19:07,918
THIS IS BEAUTIFUL.

425
00:19:07,918 --> 00:19:11,522
I WANTED TO TALK TO YOU ALL
ABOUT WHERE YOU ARE.

426
00:19:11,522 --> 00:19:13,891
LOOK AT THIS PLACE,
AND IT'S ABSOLUTELY BEAUTIFUL.

427
00:19:13,891 --> 00:19:15,426
THIS IS PARADISE.

428
00:19:15,426 --> 00:19:17,828
BUT OF COURSE, WE KNOW
THERE'S A HISTORY HERE.

429
00:19:17,828 --> 00:19:22,533
THAT HISTORY WAS DECEMBER 26TH,
2004, THE DAY AFTER CHRISTMAS.

430
00:19:22,533 --> 00:19:27,538
THE TSUNAMI HIT PHUKET,
AND IT DEVASTATED THIS ISLAND,

431
00:19:27,538 --> 00:19:29,640
AND ALMOST 6,000 PEOPLE DIED.

432
00:19:29,640 --> 00:19:32,509
WITH THE TSUNAMI, IN TOTAL,
IT AFFECTED 13 COUNTRIES,

433
00:19:32,509 --> 00:19:34,445
ABOUT A QUARTER OF A MILLION
PEOPLE DEAD.

434
00:19:34,445 --> 00:19:35,880
THAT WAS THE DEATH TOLL.

435
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:39,683
AS TYRA IS TALKING, ALL I CAN
HELP THINK ABOUT IS, LIKE,

436
00:19:39,683 --> 00:19:41,685
THE PEOPLE
WHO LOST LOVED ONES.

437
00:19:41,685 --> 00:19:45,322
AS A MODEL, YOU'RE GONNA TRAVEL
TO THE MOST BEAUTIFUL PLACES,

438
00:19:45,322 --> 00:19:48,592
BUT EVERY ISLAND,
EVERY COUNTRY HAS A STORY.

439
00:19:48,592 --> 00:19:50,828
IT'S IMPORTANT TO RESPECT
THE CULTURE

440
00:19:50,828 --> 00:19:52,763
AND TO RESPECT THE HISTORY.

441
00:19:52,763 --> 00:19:56,834
IT WAS VERY EMOTIONAL FOR ME,
BUT I'M A SOLDIER, YOU KNOW,

442
00:19:56,834 --> 00:19:58,636
AND I HELD IT TOGETHER.

443
00:19:58,636 --> 00:20:00,271
BUT I REALLY, YOU KNOW,
I THOUGHT ABOUT IT INSIDE.

444
00:20:00,271 --> 00:20:02,273
IT'S NOT ABOUT
BEING SAD TODAY.

445
00:20:02,273 --> 00:20:03,540
IT'S ABOUT
CELEBRATING THE FACT

446
00:20:03,540 --> 00:20:05,976
THAT THIS BEAUTIFUL PROVINCE
IS REBUILT.

447
00:20:05,976 --> 00:20:09,880
IT'S A SAFE PLACE, AND IT'S
A BEAUTIFUL PLACE, ALL RIGHT?

448
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:11,615
YOU KNOW WHAT I'D LIKE TO DO
WITH YOU GUYS NOW

449
